/* Đợt 6: đáp án bản mới cho Writing W01–W32 (đợt 6: W01–W19, đợt 7: W20–W32) (tài liệu "<Tên> club.docx"). W04: chỉ có dàn ý ý tưởng Part 4 – phiên bản 2. */
window.WRITING_V2={"W01": {"src": "Art Club", "p1": ["Watching movies./ I like watching movies.", "Football./ I like playing football.", "I stayed at home.", "Yes, I do./ Yes, I like shopping.", "I'm a teacher./ A teacher."], "p2": "I really like a photo of a beach at sunset. I took it during a trip with my family last summer, and the colors of the sky were beautiful.", "p3": ["I still have a small drawing that my grandmother gave me when I was a child. It is not very good, but I have kept it for more than 15 years because it means a lot to me.", "Yes, I think taking a course would be a great idea. A teacher can give you useful feedback and correct your mistakes, which is much faster than learning completely by yourself.", "I don't think street art is bad. In my opinion, it makes cities more colorful and interesting, as long as artists paint in places where it is allowed."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our art club wants to invite an artist to give a talk to attract more members. I think we should invite a street artist because it's popular with young people. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Organiser,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the art club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my ideas about the upcoming talk mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the club wants to invite an artist to talk to the members and the public. I was very excited to hear that news, because I think it is a great way to attract more people.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I suggest inviting a well-known street artist to talk about modern art, because this topic is interesting and popular with young people. Second, the artist could also give a short live painting demonstration, which would attract both young and elderly visitors.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W02": {"src": "Book Club", "p1": ["Football./ It's football.", "Watching movies./ I like watching movies.", "Football./ I like playing football.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "Playing football./ I play football with friends."], "p2": "I usually read books at home in my bedroom before going to sleep. On weekends, I sometimes read at a quiet coffee shop near my house instead.", "p3": ["My favorite time to read is late at night, when the house is quiet. I usually sit in my bedroom with a cup of tea and enjoy a good novel for an hour.", "You could ask your friend what kind of stories he likes, such as adventure or mystery. If you're not sure, a bestseller or an award-winning book is usually a safe choice.", "I don't fully agree. Although many people now read e-books, I think traditional books will always have fans who enjoy the feeling of holding a real book in their hands."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How are you? I just heard that our club wants to invite a famous author to speak at an event. I think we should invite a well-known novelist. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the book club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my ideas about the upcoming event mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, our club wants to invite a famous author to give a talk to the public. I was very excited to hear that news, because it is a wonderful opportunity for our members.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I suggest inviting a well-known novelist, because their stories are popular and interesting to a wide audience. Second, the author could talk about their writing journey and inspiration, which would be useful and motivating for members who enjoy writing.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W03": {"src": "Book Club 2", "p1": ["I like pink./ Pink.", "My hometown is Yen Bai./ Yen Bai.", "I love spring./ Spring.", "I love my house./ My house.", "19 years old./ I'm 19 years old."], "p2": "I really like reading books. It is fun and useful. It helps me relax after work, reduce stress and broaden my mind, because there are many interesting stories and useful lessons.", "p3": ["I am really interested in science books, which help me understand more about the world around us. I am curious about how things work, and science also allows us to have inventions that make our lives better.", "I usually read books after studying or at the weekend when I have free time. I often go to the library near my house because I can borrow many good books there, or sometimes go to a café instead.", "I agree that many people are too busy to read books. However, this is not good for their mental and physical health. They should make some time to relax, since reading is an easy way to reduce stress and feel better."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that the public library might close next year because not enough people go there to read. I think we should offer free books or reading events to attract more visitors. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the possible closure of the public library mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that the local authorities may close the public library next year because too few people go there to read, which would affect the whole community. To be honest, I was very sad to hear this news.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should offer free books and reading events for local people, which is practical and easy to arrange and could attract new visitors. Second, we should promote the library and its activities on Facebook, since this can reach many more people, especially young readers.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W05": {"src": "Car Club", "p1": ["Yes, I do./ I have a driving licence.", "By car./ I travel by car.", "Toyota./ I love Toyota.", "Every day./ I travel by car every day.", "My father./ My father usually drives."], "p2": "Yes, I usually travel by car. It's convenient and comfortable because I can go anywhere at any time. However, it is not affordable.", "p3": ["Last year, I went to Da Lat with my family by car. It took about 5 hours to go there. On the way, we talked or listened to music. It was really fun because we could share happy moments together", "As far as I can remember, it was about 5 years ago when I was living in Hanoi. One day when I was on the way home, my car was broken. It was terrible because it was very hot outside.", "In my opinion, we should take public transportation because it is affordable and good for the environment. We can save money for other important things. Besides, it helps reduce air pollution and traffic jams."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club needs to choose two members to represent us in the car programme in Europe, one driver and one passenger. I think we should choose the most experienced and confident drivers. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming car programme mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that our club needs to choose two representatives, one main driver and one passenger, to take part in a car programme across Europe. To be honest, I was very excited to hear that news, as it is a great opportunity for our club.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should choose members who have strong driving skills and enough experience to handle long journeys safely. Second, it is advisable to hold a short interview to select the most suitable candidates fairly.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W06": {"src": "College Club", "p1": ["My surname is Nguyen./ Nguyen.", "By bus./ I came here by bus.", "I speak Vietnamese./ Vietnamese.", "English./ I like English.", "Lan./ My best friend is Lan."], "p2": "I am free in the afternoons, and I can attend courses on Monday and Tuesday afternoon. I would like to study English, and I hope this course can help me.", "p3": ["I am studying English. I chose this course because it is very important for my future job, and if I can speak English well, I can communicate with people all over the world.", "I think the college is great. I am learning numerous useful things from well-qualified teachers and making friends with smart and studious students. I really like the environment here.", "I know that the college sports club has closed, and this is bad news for me and many others, because that is where we could play sports and share happy moments together."], "p4": ["Hi Dan,\nI just heard that our exams have been moved two weeks earlier, from the 21st to the 7th of next month. I think we should start revising together right away. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you soon", "Dear Administrator,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming exam schedule mentioned in the recent email from the college.\nI have been informed that the end-of-course exams will now take place two weeks earlier, moving from the 21st to the 7th of next month. To be honest, I was quite worried to hear that news, as students now have less time to prepare.\nBeing a student of the college, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should have an online meeting for students to express their concerns directly to the administration, as it is fast and easy to carry out. Second, we should ask lecturers to provide extra revision sessions before the new exam date, as this would help students prepare more effectively.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to the college.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W07": {"src": "Community Club", "p1": ["In Da Nang./ I live in Da Nang.", "Seafood./ I like seafood.", "Nguyen./ My surname is Nguyen.", "Vietnamese./ I speak Vietnamese.", "At 11 pm./ I go to bed at 11 pm."], "p2": "I live in a small apartment in the city center, near a park. It is quiet and convenient, because there are many shops and a bus stop nearby.", "p3": ["I usually help my neighbors by carrying heavy things or looking after their children when they are busy. I also help elderly people cross the street or carry their bags sometimes.", "I suggest starting with something simple, like donating clothes or books to a local charity. You could also join a volunteer group at a shelter, since it is an easy and meaningful way to begin.", "Yes, I think teenagers should volunteer during school holidays. It teaches them responsibility and empathy, and it also gives them valuable experience that can be useful for their studies and future careers."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club is planning two community projects. I think we should choose the sports facilities project because it helps more young people. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the community club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the club is planning to choose between building sports facilities for young people or parks for the elderly. I was very interested to hear that news, because both projects sound very meaningful.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I think the club should choose the sports facilities project, because it can help children and young people improve their health, keep fit and prevent health problems. Second, the club could also call for support from the local government, since parks for the elderly could be built later with extra funding.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W08": {"src": "Computer Club", "p1": ["Blue./ It's blue.", "Swimming./ I like swimming.", "Winter./ I like winter.", "Playing games./ I like playing games.", "Cloudy and cold./ It's cloudy and cold."], "p2": "I usually use a computer at home in the evening, after I finish my homework. I use it to chat with friends, watch videos and sometimes do some online shopping.", "p3": ["Last week I used a computer to book train tickets for a trip with my family. It was very quick and convenient, and I did not have to queue at the station.", "Your grandmother could start with simple things, like video calls and online games. You could also give her a short lesson every week and be patient, because it takes time to learn something new.", "I agree that some young people use computers too much. However, if they use it for studying or communicating with friends and family, I think it is not really a bad thing."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club is planning to redesign the website to attract more members. I think we should add more photos and videos of our activities. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the computer club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming changes to our website mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the website is going to be redesigned to attract more visitors. I was very happy to hear that news, because I think our current website is too simple.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should add more photos and short videos of our club activities, because this will make the website look more attractive. Second, we should promote the website on social networking sites such as Facebook, because it can reach a lot more people.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W09": {"src": "Debate Club", "p1": ["Summer./ I like summer.", "Football./ I like football.", "Da Nang./ I want to go to Da Nang.", "Sunny and warm./ It's sunny and warm.", "Watching movies./ I like watching movies."], "p2": "With my friends, I usually talk about school, music and sports. We also talk about films we have watched and share our opinions about the news.", "p3": ["I usually follow the news on social media and news apps on my phone. I also watch the news on TV every evening with my family to know what is happening around the world.", "Congratulations on your debate! I think you should practice in front of a mirror first and speak slowly and clearly. Try to look at the audience and stay calm, and it will help you make a good impression.", "Yes, I agree with you. Before making a decision, it is important to think about both sides of an argument. This way, we can avoid mistakes and make a fairer, more reasonable decision."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club wants more young people to join. I think we should organize some fun debate games and invite guest speakers to make it more interesting. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear President,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the debate club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my ideas about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, many young people think that debating is not their thing. I was a bit worried to hear that news, because I think debating is very useful for everyone.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, debating helps us improve our public speaking skills and confidence, which are very useful for our studies and future jobs. Second, it helps us think more critically, because we learn to consider different sides of an issue before giving an opinion.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W10": {"src": "English Club", "p1": ["I'm a student./ A student.", "Summer./ I like summer.", "Blue./ It's blue.", "Reading books./ I like reading books.", "Sunny and warm./ It's sunny and warm."], "p2": "I use English every day at school and when I watch English movies or listen to music. I also chat with some foreign friends online in English.", "p3": ["I also found English difficult at school, but I improved a lot by watching English movies with subtitles and practicing speaking with friends every day. A private teacher can really help you too.", "I think the best way to improve speaking is to practice every day, even by talking to yourself. You could also join a speaking club or find a language partner online to practice with.", "I agree that communication is more important than being perfect. Making mistakes is a normal part of learning, and we should not be afraid to speak just because we are not sure."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club wants to organize an event to attract more members. I think we should have an English movie night with games. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the English club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my ideas about the upcoming event mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the club wants to organize an event to attract more members of all ages. I was very excited to hear that news, because I think it is a great opportunity for our club.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I suggest an English movie night, because it is fun and attracts young people. Second, we could also add simple English quiz games with small prizes, since this could attract both young and older members.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W11": {"src": "English Club 2", "p1": ["My mother./ It's my mother.", "By car./ I travel by car.", "Vietnamese./ It's Vietnamese.", "Pop music./ It's pop music.", "At 10 pm./ I go to bed at 10 pm."], "p2": "I usually use the Internet to learn online, watch movies, listen to music and play games. Sometimes, I use the Internet to chat with my friends. Every day, I use the Internet for work and online study. Sometimes, I use it to listen to music with my family, which helps me relax.", "p3": ["I usually spend only 2 hours learning English. I learn English by watching movies and reading books in English. Sometimes, I also practice speaking with English-speaking friends I meet online. I join an English club where I can practice speaking English with people from different countries. It's really useful for me because it helps me improve my English fast and effectively.", "I totally agree with this idea. English is the international language which is spoken all over the world. It helps us communicate with people from different countries and get good jobs.", "I usually use English in class, where I have to speak English with teachers and friends. Sometimes, I use English to speak with some of my friends who come from different countries."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Mary. How's it going? Did you get the latest email about new words and phrases? I think new words are interesting and fun. Some people have strong reactions to this issue because they are old and they don't like changes. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nCatch you later.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I have been an active member of the club for six months. I am writing this email regarding the issue mentioned in the recent announcement from our club.\nI have been informed that nowadays more and more new words and phrases are added to the language, so many people have strong reactions to this issue. Some people like new words and phrases because they are interesting and fun, and language would become boring without them. Others, especially older people, do not like the changes.\nIn my opinion, we can accept some new words and phrases because they can make the language more colourful. However, there should be certain rules, and we should not accept words that can cause bad feelings.\nHopefully, my ideas will be helpful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W12": {"src": "Fashion Club", "p1": ["I am wearing a dress./ A T-shirt and jeans.", "4 people./ Four people.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "By car./ I walk to school.", "I like reading books./ My hobby is reading books."], "p2": "The last time I went shopping for clothes was last week. I bought a T-shirt and a pair of jeans from a shop. They were very beautiful. Last week I bought a sweater and a jacket from a shop near my house. They cost 300 dollars, but I really liked them because they were fashionable and stylish.", "p3": ["I prefer to buy online because it is convenient. I don't have to go to stores to buy clothes. I can stay at home and order, which can save me a lot of time. I prefer buying clothes online for some reasons. First, it is more convenient as I don't have to go to stores, so I can save time. Second, I can buy things at low prices with discounts or vouchers.", "I decided to join the club because I love fashion and I want to meet people who share my hobby. I think I can learn a lot of things from them. I decided to take part in the club because I find a lot of interest in fashion and I would like to meet the club members who share my hobby.", "People like fashion because it can make them look more beautiful and confident about themselves. Besides, it can show their personalities and creativity, and it also helps them express their own unique style. People are interested in fashion for some reasons. The first reason is that fashion allows them to look better, so they feel more confident. Another reason is that it can show their creativity."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club is planning to hold meetings with famous designers, either online or as a fashion show. I think we should choose the online meetings because they're more convenient for everyone. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming event mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that our club is planning meetings with famous designers and needs feedback on whether to hold them online or as a fashion-show-style event. To be honest, I was very excited to hear that news.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I believe the meetings should be held online, since it is more convenient for designers who live in other countries and saves travel costs. Second, we should promote the event on Facebook, because it can reach more members and attract more interest.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W13": {"src": "Film Club", "p1": ["Vietnam./ I am from Vietnam.", "I like to read books./ Reading books.", "It's sunny./ Sunny.", "In the evening./ I study in the evening.", "Yes, I do./ Yes, I like dancing."], "p2": "I watch movies in the living room with my family at the weekend or in the evening. It's fun and relaxing after a long, busy week.", "p3": ["Yesterday I watched a movie with my friends at the cinema. It was a cartoon about a cat and a mouse. It was very funny, and I laughed from the beginning to the end.", "To avoid falling asleep when watching movies, I think you should drink coffee or tea before the film starts. Also, you can eat some snacks or talk to other people to stay awake and focused.", "Your question is interesting, but I don't fully agree. I don't think we should avoid black-and-white films, because we can understand more about the technology, culture and life in the past through them."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club is going to have a meeting and invite a famous film critic to speak. I think we should invite Mr. David and ask him to talk about \"Movies Today\". What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming meeting mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that our club is planning a meeting and will invite a famous film critic to give a talk. To be honest, I was so excited to hear that news, as I have been looking forward to an event like this for a long time.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I recommend inviting Mr. David, a well-known film critic in our city who has both experience and expertise. Second, I suggest the talk should focus on the topic \"Movies Today\", as it is interesting and can attract more members, both young and old.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W14": {"src": "Fitness Club 1", "p1": ["I'm fine, thanks./ Fine, thanks.", "Summer./ I like summer.", "Sunny and hot./ It's sunny and hot.", "Swimming./ I like swimming.", "Playing football./ I like playing football."], "p2": "I decided to join the club because I want to keep fit and lose some weight. I also want to make new friends who enjoy exercising too.", "p3": ["To keep fit, I usually go jogging every morning before work. I also try to eat healthy food and drink a lot of water every day. Sometimes I play badminton with my friends at the weekend too.", "Yes, I prefer getting up early to go for a run. The air is fresh in the morning, and it also helps me feel more energetic for the rest of the day.", "I agree that technology makes life easier, but I don't think we are too lazy because of it. Many people still make time to exercise, even with a busy schedule."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that the club equipment is too old and the club may increase the membership fee by 50%. I think we should organize a sponsor event instead. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear President,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the fitness club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, our club equipment is too old and needs to be replaced. I was quite worried to hear that news, especially about the plan to increase the membership fee by 50%.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I think we should organize a sponsor event instead of raising the fee, because a higher fee may discourage many members from staying in the club. Second, we could ask local businesses for help, since it is a fast and practical way to raise money for new equipment.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W15": {"src": "Fitness Club 2", "p1": ["Fried rice./ I like fried rice.", "Blue./ It's blue.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "Playing football./ I like playing football.", "Football./ Football is the most popular."], "p2": "Last week, I had to run to the bus stop because I was late for work. I was very tired when I finally arrived, but I managed to catch the bus.", "p3": ["I heard about the Health club from a close friend who is already a member. She told me that the facilities are good and the instructors are very friendly and helpful.", "I want to lose some weight and become healthier when I join the club. I would also like to make new friends who enjoy exercising and can encourage me to keep going.", "I think the facilities in the gym are quite good, but some machines are old and need to be repaired. Apart from that, the gym is clean and has enough space for everyone."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our instructors will be away for two weeks. I think we should follow online workout videos to keep exercising safely. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the fitness club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, our instructors will be absent for the next two weeks. I was a little worried to hear that news, since I usually need some guidance during my workouts.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some suggestions. First, the club could share some simple online workout videos for members to follow safely during this time. Second, experienced members could help and support beginners, since this is a fast and easy way to solve the problem.\nHopefully, my suggestions will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W16": {"src": "Food Club", "p1": ["Dogs./ I like dogs.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "Summer./ I like summer.", "I'm a student./ A student.", "English./ I like English."], "p2": "I usually eat my meals at home with my family in the evening. Sometimes on weekends, I go out to eat at a restaurant with my friends instead.", "p3": ["Last month I had a delicious seafood dinner at a small restaurant near the beach with my family. The food was fresh and tasty, and we all really enjoyed the meal together.", "I recommend a small street food stall near my house that sells banh mi. The bread is crispy, and the filling is always fresh, so it is very popular with local people.", "I agree that fast food is not very healthy, but many people still eat it because it is quick and convenient. I think people should try to cook more meals at home."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club needs volunteers to give a short talk about food. I think I will talk about street food in Vietnam because it's interesting. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the food club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming talks mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the club needs volunteers to give a short talk about food. I was very excited to hear that news, because I love sharing my ideas about food with other members.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I would like to talk about street food in Vietnam, because it is cheap, tasty and part of our culture. Second, I could also talk about healthy eating habits, since it is a useful topic for everyone in the club.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W17": {"src": "Home living Club", "p1": ["In Hanoi./ I live in Hanoi.", "The living room./ I like the living room.", "4 people./ There are 4 people.", "Blue./ I like blue.", "At 6 pm./ I get home at 6 pm."], "p2": "I live in a house in Hanoi. There are 5 rooms: a living room, a kitchen, two bedrooms and a bathroom. It is small but beautiful, and I really like it.", "p3": ["I feel happy because it is fun and useful. We can talk and share everything in life. Also, it is economical, because we can save both money and space.", "I don't agree with this idea. In the countryside, the air is fresh and good for our health. The food is delicious and cheap, and the people are friendly and kind.", "I think some old buildings are not safe for the people living there, so they should be demolished and replaced with modern ones. New buildings are usually more beautiful and comfortable."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club wants to help young families find houses or apartments to buy. I think we should connect them with local real estate agents. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to share my opinions about the upcoming plan mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that many young families are looking for a house to buy, and our club wants members to help them. To be honest, I was very happy to hear that news, because it is a meaningful project.\nI would like to offer two ideas. First, we should hold an online meeting for members to share useful information, as it is fast and easy to carry out. Second, we should ask an expert in real estate for help, since this is the best way to give reliable advice.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W18": {"src": "Museum Club", "p1": ["Sunny and warm./ It's sunny and warm.", "A blue shirt./ I'm wearing a blue shirt.", "Pop music./ I like pop music.", "Football./ I like football.", "Watching movies./ I like watching movies."], "p2": "Last month, I went to the History Museum with my class. We saw many interesting old objects, and our teacher explained the history behind each one.", "p3": ["When I was a child, I visited the museum with my school every year. I remember feeling amazed by the huge dinosaur bones, and I always looked forward to those school trips.", "I think the History Museum would be a better choice for your children, because it has more interactive activities and colorful displays that are usually more interesting for young children.", "I think technology attracts more visitors because it makes learning more interesting and fun. For example, computer screens can show videos and games that explain the history behind each object."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our museum may start charging an entrance fee next year. I think we should keep it free to avoid losing visitors. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear President,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the museum club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the museum may start charging tickets next year, which could decrease the number of visitors. I was quite worried to hear that news, since the museum is currently very popular because it is free.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some suggestions. First, I think we should not charge a fee, because it may cause inconvenience and discourage regular visitors. Second, if money is really needed, we could simply ask for optional donations instead, since this is a fair and practical solution.\nHopefully, my suggestions will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W19": {"src": "Music Club 1", "p1": ["I love tennis./ Tennis.", "There are 4 people./ 4 people.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "By bus./ I go to school by bus.", "It is reading books./ Reading books."], "p2": "The last time I listened to music was last night when I came home from work. I listened to a song which is very popular right now.", "p3": ["I listen to music every day, as it is really relaxing and enjoyable. I often listen to music with my friends in a café near my house. They often play my favourite songs.", "You could talk to your son about the benefits of learning music, or take him to a café or theatre where they play music. I think he will like it once he tries.", "I agree that music reflects cultural differences. It is true that when we hear a piece of music, we can often guess its country of origin, because it can serve as a symbol of a culture."], "p4": ["Hi Tom,\nI just heard that residents living near our club have been complaining about the noise from our concerts. I think we should hold the concerts earlier in the evening instead. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the noise problem mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that residents living near our club have complained about the noise from our concerts. To be honest, I was quite worried to hear that news, as it could damage our club's reputation.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should have an online meeting so members can discuss possible solutions directly, which is fast and easy to carry out. Second, it is advisable for us to install soundproofing devices or hold concerts in a venue further from residential areas, so as not to disturb the neighbourhood.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W04": {"src": "Business Club", "note": "Offer free courses to support local universities nearby.\n(I think the club should offer free courses because they can provide useful knowledge and skills for students who want to start a small business. This is practical and affordable to carry out because many people can join without worrying about the cost. Therefore, the club can support local individuals and build a stronger relationship with the community.)\nInvite successful business owners to share their experience in the courses.\n(I think the club should invite famous or successful business owners to give talks because they have experience and expertise in this field. They can share useful advice about starting a business. Therefore, participants can learn practical skills and feel more confident about their future plans.)", "p4v": 1}, "W20": {"src": "Music club 2", "p1": ["I was born in Hanoi./ In Hanoi.", "I love reading books./ My hobby is playing sports.", "At 8 am./ I have breakfast at 8 am.", "I'm 40 years old./ 40 years old.", "Twice a week./ I go shopping twice a week."], "p2": "I usually listen to music at home in the evening. Sometimes I listen to music in a coffee shop at the weekend. I often enjoy music with some close friends in a nice café in the city at the weekend. It's enjoyable, and it helps me relax after a busy week.", "p3": ["When I was small, I lived with my grandmother. She often read stories to me before I went to bed. I really loved the stories she read. They were very interesting and useful. When I was small, I lived with my aunt, and she took care of me. She often read stories to me before bedtime. I really loved the fairy stories she read. They were very interesting and meaningful.", "I agree with this idea, because it can badly affect many people. Some people cannot bear loud music, and some are trying to focus on their work. Others may want to sleep. I totally agree with this idea, because it can seriously affect people around us, especially elderly people and children. Some cannot bear loud music, and others are trying to concentrate on their work.", "I strongly agree with this idea. In my country, older people often listen to classical music or bolero songs, while young people love rock, pop or remix music. I strongly agree with this idea, because people of different ages love different kinds of music. Older people often listen to classical or country music, while young people are more interested in pop or rock music."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club is going to organise a music concert for both young and old members. I think we should offer free tickets to attract more people. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming music concert mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that our club is going to organise a music concert to attract both young and old members. To be honest, I was very excited to hear that news, as this will be our first big event.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should offer free tickets or a big discount for families, including grandparents, parents and children, as this is practical and easy to do. Second, it is advisable for us to vary the music played, mixing classical and modern songs, so that everyone can enjoy the concert.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W21": {"src": "Nature club", "p1": ["I speak Vietnamese./ Vietnamese.", "I love cats./ Cats.", "I enjoy watching TV./ Watching TV.", "Twice a week./ I go shopping twice a week.", "It was last Sunday./ Last Sunday."], "p2": "I enjoy playing sports. I often play soccer with my friends at the weekend. It's fun and helpful, because it helps me relax, improve my health and keep fit.", "p3": ["I like to visit Ha Long Bay. It's the most popular travel destination in Vietnam, with beautiful islands, mountains and caves. There, we can do interesting things like swimming in the sea, climbing the mountains and visiting caves.", "I decided to take part in the club because I love the beauty of nature, and I would like to meet people who share the same hobby. I think we can share a lot of experiences together.", "It is true that the bigger the club, the more environmentally conscious people become. Nowadays, more and more people are interested in the environment, because it directly affects our lives."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club is planning to encourage young people to spend more time outdoors instead of staying home playing games. I think we should organise fun activities like camping or sports days. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming plan mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that our club is planning to encourage young people to spend more time outdoors instead of staying at home playing games. To be honest, I was very happy to hear that news, because it is good for their health.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should organise interesting outdoor activities such as camping, hiking or sports events, since these are fun and keep young people active. Second, we should educate people about the importance of spending time outdoors, as this is the most effective solution in the long term.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W22": {"src": "Photography club", "p1": ["Yes, I do./ Yes, I like shopping.", "Check my emails./ I usually check my emails.", "Dogs./ I like dogs.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "Summer./ I like summer."], "p2": "I like taking photographs early in the morning at the beach, when the light is soft and beautiful. I also enjoy taking photos during family trips.", "p3": ["My favorite family photo is a picture of my grandparents' wedding day. It is very old, but I love it because it shows how happy and young they looked at that time.", "I enjoy taking photos of nature, especially mountains and rivers during my trips. I like these photos because they remind me of the peaceful and beautiful places I have visited.", "I think it depends on the situation. Taking photos of yourself can be a nice way to remember special moments, but doing it too often can also be a little bit annoying."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club may add separate photo categories for men, women and people under 16. I think it's a great idea. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear President,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the photography club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the proposed change mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the club is thinking about having separate competition categories instead of just one. I was very pleased to hear that news, because I think it is a fair and positive change.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I support the new categories, because it gives everyone, especially younger photographers, a fairer chance to win. Second, this change could also encourage more women and young people to join the competition.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W23": {"src": "Photography club 2", "p1": ["In Hanoi./ I live in Hanoi.", "Yes, I am./ I am married.", "2 months./ For 2 months.", "I always watch TV./ Watching TV.", "I practised some English lessons./ I studied English."], "p2": "The last time I took a photo was yesterday. I took some nice photos with my best friend when we had a trip to Ho Guom Lake.", "p3": ["I usually store my photos on my laptop because it is convenient and easy for me to look at them when I want to recall happy moments with my best friends and my relatives.", "I think photographers can get more inspiration for taking interesting pictures by using the Internet, since a lot of people post videos and pictures there that can spark new ideas.", "I think photographers need to be creative and hard-working to become successful, since these qualities help them come up with interesting ideas and create amazing photos. As a result, more people will get to know their work."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club's photo contest will now have separate categories for women, men and children this year. I think this is a great change. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming contest mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that this year's contest will be divided into separate categories for women, men and children under 16. To be honest, I was very happy to hear that news, since it makes the competition fairer for everyone.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should promote the new contest on social networking sites, especially Facebook, because it can reach more people and attract more entries. Second, we should offer free entry for children under 16, as this is a practical way to encourage young members to join.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W24": {"src": "Power fitness club", "p1": ["Football./ I like football.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "Playing football./ I like playing football.", "Yes, I do./ Yes, I like shopping.", "Check my emails./ I usually check my emails."], "p2": "I want to try different sports and get fitter this year. I am usually free to exercise in the evening after work, from around 6 to 8 pm.", "p3": ["Hi Amy, thanks for the warm welcome! I joined the club because I want to get fitter and try some new sports. I'm really looking forward to meeting everyone here.", "I understand how busy life can be. I suggest doing short 20-minute workouts a few times a week instead of long sessions, and try to exercise at a time that fits your schedule.", "I think more people are interested in keeping fit because they want to stay healthy and reduce stress from busy modern life. Social media also makes fitness look more popular nowadays."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How are you? I just heard that our club needs to cut costs, so it might close the shop or the cafe. I think we should close the shop instead. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the power fitness club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the club needs to cut costs by closing either the shop or the cafe. I was a little sad to hear that news, but I understand that it is necessary.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some suggestions. First, I think we should close the shop, because most members buy sports equipment outside the club anyway. Second, we should keep the cafe, since many members like to relax and chat there after training.\nHopefully, my suggestions will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W25": {"src": "Reading club", "p1": ["Sunny and warm./ It's sunny and warm.", "Autumn./ I like autumn.", "Reading the news./ I like reading the news.", "Reading books./ I like reading books.", "I'm a teacher./ A teacher."], "p2": "I read a mystery novel last weekend. It was really exciting, and I finished it in just two days because I could not stop thinking about the ending.", "p3": ["I enjoy reading mystery and adventure novels because they keep me curious about what will happen next. I also like biographies, since they teach me interesting lessons from other people's real lives.", "I suggest taking short notes or highlighting important points while you read. Reviewing your notes once a week can also help you remember the information for a much longer time.", "Yes, I think it is a little worrying, because reading helps develop imagination and knowledge. However, parents can encourage children by choosing fun, colorful books that are easy to enjoy."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club wants to help redesign the national library. I think we should suggest adding a cozy reading corner with comfortable chairs. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the reading club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my ideas about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, the library needs to become more modern and exciting to attract both young and old visitors. I was very excited to hear that news, because I think this is a great opportunity to change how people see libraries.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, the library could add a cozy reading corner with comfortable chairs and soft lighting, to make it more relaxing. Second, it could also organize free workshops and book clubs for different age groups, since this would attract more visitors regularly.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W26": {"src": "Science club", "p1": ["I'm an engineer./ An engineer.", "I stayed at home./ Home.", "Blue./ It's blue.", "Reading books./ I like reading books.", "Sunny and warm./ It's sunny and warm."], "p2": "I usually read science books at home in the evening, after finishing my work. I especially enjoy reading about space and new technology on weekends.", "p3": ["I remember my science teacher doing fun experiments in class, which made me very interested in the subject. Since then, I have always enjoyed learning how things work in the world around us.", "I also enjoy reading science books more than watching scientific programmes. I think books explain things in more detail, and I can read at my own pace and think about the ideas.", "I agree that technology can have a negative effect, for example making people less active. However, I think the benefits, such as easier communication and access to information, are much greater."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club is planning a science exhibition next month. I think we should include fun hands-on experiments for children. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the science club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my ideas about the upcoming exhibition mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, our club will hold a science exhibition for the public next month. I was very excited to hear that news, because it is a great chance to share our love of science.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I suggest including fun, hands-on experiments, because this will attract both children and adults. Second, I think the exhibition should be free of charge, since a fee may discourage some families from coming.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W28": {"src": "Technology club", "p1": ["I'm a student./ A student.", "Green./ It's green.", "Pizza./ I like pizza.", "Check my emails./ I usually check my emails.", "I stayed at home./ Home."], "p2": "I usually use a computer for studying and doing research for school. I also use it to watch videos, chat with friends and sometimes play online games.", "p3": ["Yes, once my laptop suddenly stopped working right before an important deadline. I was very stressed, but luckily I had saved my work online, so I did not lose anything important.", "I prefer watching films online because it is more convenient and cheaper. I can watch whenever I want, and I don't have to travel to the cinema or wait in a queue.", "I agree that technology has made life easier in many ways, such as communication and work. However, I think it can also make people less active and more dependent on machines."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club is thinking about changing the online system so that comments are no longer anonymous. I think it is a good idea. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the technology club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the situation mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, some members are posting negative comments anonymously on our system. I was quite disappointed to hear that news, because it is not a respectful way to communicate.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I think we should change the system so that everyone's name is shown, because people will think twice before posting something negative. Second, we should also set clear rules about acceptable online behavior, since this will be the most effective solution in the long term.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W29": {"src": "Television club", "p1": ["A blue shirt./ I'm wearing a blue shirt.", "Pop music./ I like pop music.", "Football./ I like football.", "Dogs./ I like dogs.", "Sunny and warm./ It's sunny and warm."], "p2": "I usually watch TV in the evening after dinner. I mostly watch the news and some comedy shows, because they help me relax after a long day.", "p3": ["I usually relax while watching TV by lying on my bed with some snacks. It helps me forget about work and enjoy some free time before going to sleep.", "I prefer watching TV with my family. It is more fun to share opinions about the show together, and we can also spend some quality time as a family.", "I agree that children shouldn't watch too much TV. It is better for them to spend more time reading, playing outside and studying instead of sitting in front of a screen."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nIt's me, Linda. How's it going? I just heard that our club is going to hold an annual meeting. I think we should hold it on a Saturday evening at the community hall. What do you think? Let's talk about it later.\nSee you soon.", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Linda. I have been an active member of the television club for 6 months. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming annual meeting mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nAccording to the email, our club is planning to hold an annual meeting soon. I was very happy to hear that news, because it is a great chance for members to meet each other.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, I think we should hold the meeting on a Saturday evening, because most members are free to attend at that time. Second, it is better to hold it at the community hall near the club, since it is convenient and easy for everyone to find.\nHopefully, my ideas will be useful for our club. I am looking forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W30": {"src": "Travel club", "p1": ["I love cats and dogs./ Cats and dogs.", "I get up at 6 am./ At 6 am.", "I speak English./ English.", "There are 4 people./ 4 people.", "I really like coffee./ Yes, I do."], "p2": "I am interested in travel because it is interesting and useful. It helps me relax and reduce stress. Besides, it allows me to broaden my mind and improve my knowledge. I find a lot of interest in travel because travelling is enjoyable and beneficial. It helps me relax and reduce stress, and it improves my knowledge of the world.", "p3": ["I had a trip in bad weather two years ago when I visited Ha Long Bay with my family. It started to rain heavily while we were on the boat, and we were scared, but the tour guide reassured us.", "I totally agree with this statement. Some kinds of transportation for long distances, like airplanes, trains, ships or cars, can seriously pollute the air and water, which can directly affect people's health.", "There are many popular tourist attractions in my country, including Ha Long Bay, Da Lat and Hanoi. There, visitors can enjoy the beauty of nature, try local food, explore new places and meet hospitable people."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club is preparing to welcome a group of foreign tourists who don't speak Vietnamese. I think we should hire an interpreter to help us communicate with them. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the visit mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that our club is preparing to welcome a group of foreign tourists visiting our country for the first time, and they do not speak Vietnamese. To be honest, I was so happy to hear that news, because it is a great chance to practise my English and share our culture.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should ask for help from an expert, such as a professional interpreter, to help us communicate with them. It is the best way to avoid misunderstandings. Second, we should organize a welcome party so the tourists feel comfortable in our country.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W31": {"src": "Walking club – phone", "p1": ["My surname is Nguyen./ Nguyen.", "I live in Vietnam./ Vietnam.", "There are four people./ Four people.", "I like watching movies./ Watching movies.", "It is Justin Bieber./ Justin Bieber."], "p2": "I often walk in the park near my house. Here I can enjoy fresh air and do some exercise. It's relaxing and beneficial for my health.", "p3": ["Yes, I often go for a walk too, usually in the early morning before work. It helps me feel fresh and energetic for the rest of the day, and I really enjoy the peaceful atmosphere.", "I totally agree with you. Walking in the countryside is much more relaxing, because the air is fresh and there is less traffic and noise. Walking in the city can feel stressful and unhealthy.", "I think it's because life is busier now, and people rely on cars, motorbikes and public transport to save time. Also, many people spend their free time on their phones instead of moving around."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club wants suggestions about members using their phones while walking instead of paying attention. I think we should encourage everyone to keep their phones away during walks. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the issue mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that many members use their phones while walking instead of focusing on the activity. To be honest, I was quite concerned to hear that news, because it could be dangerous, especially near busy roads.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should remind members to keep their phones in their pockets during walks, since this is simple and easy to follow. Second, we could organize phone-free walking sessions to help members build the habit of paying full attention to their surroundings.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W32": {"src": "Walking club – Europe", "p1": ["My surname is Nguyen./ Nguyen.", "I live in Vietnam./ Vietnam.", "There are four people./ Four people.", "I like watching movies./ Watching movies.", "It is Justin Bieber./ Justin Bieber."], "p2": "I often walk in the park near my house. Here I can enjoy fresh air and do some exercise. It's relaxing and beneficial for my health.", "p3": ["The last time I walked was yesterday morning. I got up early and went to the park with my children. We walked for about 30 minutes before I went home and started my work.", "There are some ways to encourage people to walk more. First, we can educate people about the health benefits of walking. Second, we can organize walking events with attractive prizes.", "I prefer slow walking because it is more comfortable. Also, I can watch the trees and flowers along the road, listen to the birds sing and talk with other people."], "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nI just heard that our club is planning to organize a walk across European countries. I think we should tell the manager that this plan is unrealistic. What do you think? Let's talk about it over lunch.\nSee you later", "Dear Manager,\nMy name is Mary. I am writing this email to express my opinions about the upcoming plan mentioned in the recent email from our club.\nI have been informed that the club is planning to organize a walk across European countries. To be honest, I was quite worried to hear that news, because the plan seems very unrealistic and risky for most members.\nBeing a member of the club, I would like to offer some ideas. First, we should have a meeting for members to express their ideas directly about a safer, shorter route instead, since it is fast and easy to carry out. Second, we should set clear rules about distance and safety, as this is the most effective solution in the long term.\nI hope my ideas will be useful to our club.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}, "W27": {"src": "Social Club (bài giảng Ms Mai Hien)", "p4": ["Hi Jane,\nWow, I just heard that our club is planning to organize some monthly face-to-face meetings. I'm so excited — especially because I'll get to meet other club members.\nI think it would be better if we meet at the club on Sundays. What do you think? I'm planning to write to the manager and share my ideas.\nSee you soon!", "Dear Manager,\nI have got the email regarding the upcoming face-to-face meetings. I am truly to hear that because it will be a great opportunity/chance for me to meet other club members and share our experiences/stories.\nTo make the plan/meetings successful, I would like to offer some ideas. It is advisable for us to organize the meetings at the weekend/on Sunday because most people do not work at that time. Additionally, it would be a good idea to meet at the club because it is convenient for everyone to come here (at Lenin Park because it is big/spacious and beautiful. Everyone can enjoy fresh air).\nIf you have any questions or need further information, please contact me at 13465767 or via maihien@gmail.com. I look forward to hearing from you.\nBest regards"], "p4v": 0}};
WRITING_TESTS.forEach(t=>{if(WRITING_V2[t.id])t.v2=WRITING_V2[t.id];});
